Cell["The greedy path runs over its four tensors directly:", "Text",
 CellID->1678275947,ExpressionUUID->"1b4e2dea-4a49-bf2e-4975-c4b46ffd0274"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"GreedyContractionPath", "[", "tnH", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[22]:= ",
 CellID->1612195498,ExpressionUUID->"10b057f0-cb39-4e6e-4040-4ebdeecc14b4"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"2", ",", "3"}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"2", ",", "3"}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"1", ",", "2"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[22]= ",
 CellID->1847126558,ExpressionUUID->"41c6bfc6-0792-5005-77fd-36a0b227236f"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Three steps over four operands: whichever step first joins two of ",
 Cell[BoxData["t2"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "62752e4e-571f-d961-120a-c02862aba84b"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData["t3"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "34ee5221-bb14-cc46-5c96-4b8b3ea696ac"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData["t4"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "166277e1-e8de-815f-3e12-6eca8968d3a5"],
 " keeps ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0ae7a534-7379-468c-3a9c-3d7e060c2cd6"],
 ", because the third still carries it, and the step that brings in the third \
sums it."
}], "Text",
 CellID->746824257,ExpressionUUID->"34baef30-7963-b757-5c59-077a78171dbd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The other representation inserts an explicit delta \"spider\" tensor, so \
that the hyperedge becomes ordinary two-tensor bonds. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["BinaryTensorNetwork"]], 
    "paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/BinaryTensorNetwork", 
    "Wolfram/TensorNetworks Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "15ce0314-20ee-2b64-43f5-9b5e509b764e"],
 " builds it, raising the operand count from four to five:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->966663717,ExpressionUUID->"38a9ac88-4644-6c0e-6856-45d273f13754"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"BinaryTensorNetwork", "[", "tnH", "]"}], "[", "\"\<Size\>\"", 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[23]:= ",
 CellID->1320129761,ExpressionUUID->"64802aa2-b136-451c-0cbf-c30fc0c32c66"],

Cell[BoxData["5"], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[23]= ",
 CellID->1479724538,ExpressionUUID->"67771ff6-ea2e-a98b-0d0c-96b38fd8fbd1"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A path planned over the binarized network has four steps over five \
operands, and it is still accepted: a path whose operand count is that of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"BinaryTensorNetwork", "[", "tnH", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "233ecb8e-17f3-8d32-52c5-e2e8a187d418"],
 " rather than of ",
 Cell[BoxData["tnH"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7dd949a9-d8cf-50b3-2be7-60f2d97a2299"],
 " runs on the binarized network. So a contracted hyperedge has three \
equivalent representations: one ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4a74bc9f-39f4-5114-7a0b-35d9bf81207e"],
 "-element group in the global-slot convention (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["TensorContract"]], "paclet:ref/TensorContract"},
   "RefLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "598f41e5-f1df-a461-0fb5-58ce806b0f4b"],
 "), a batch index carried by the pairwise steps of a path, or an explicit \
delta spider plus pairwise bonds. The batch index is the one that scales: a \
spider's rank grows with the number of tensors on its index, so an index \
shared by two hundred tensors is a rank-200 delta, while a batch index never \
makes a step larger than its result."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1607396713,ExpressionUUID->"1e0f0df5-2071-c96f-4634-a4bf51059bb5"],

Cell["Where this leaves us", "Section",
 CellID->171231949,ExpressionUUID->"7f6e12d5-e3b9-0bb9-2515-8b9e964c5983"],

Cell["\<\
We built one network and read its indices in every convention the kernel uses:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->820919957,ExpressionUUID->"41ecc127-3c02-05fa-7793-d881b5b76fc0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A repeated ",
 Cell[BoxData["EinsteinSummation"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1190ff72-a9fe-60f8-47af-f73fcf8b32c2"],
 " label that is summed becomes one ",
 Cell[BoxData["TensorContract"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "19c80315-d7de-7125-4ff7-9b5ee26b400f"],
 " group of its global slots (a pair for two tensors, an ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6fdf78a7-59a9-97d9-15e5-7101585dfd23"],
 "-element group for more); a once-only label is a free slot."
}], "Item",
 CellID->1006830744,ExpressionUUID->"7a87483f-bfa4-2eb6-2abd-62793a51749c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The ",
 Cell[BoxData["TensorNetwork"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "09b26917-59e6-8729-3f41-81515f90ea73"],
 " data labels tag each leg with its tensor position and label; shared labels \
are bond groups, once-only labels are the free indices and set the output \
order."
}], "Item",
 CellID->1175763064,ExpressionUUID->"521ad179-838d-ce9b-0239-c923363994e1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A contraction path numbers operands and lists pairwise steps in order; \
reading the nested ",
 Cell[BoxData["ArrayDot"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "136d7364-bcfb-8461-4113-6b4e348fef4b"],
 " (or the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["ContractionTree"]], 
    "paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/ContractionTree", 
    "Wolfram/TensorNetworks Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "2b78534b-7a52-d624-5918-4b157fe4bd0e"],
 ") gives the sequence, and the legs summed at a step are recovered from the \
data."
}], "Item",
 CellID->1074416020,ExpressionUUID->"30c454b2-bdb8-e427-60fc-4dfc3432cf0d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData["ArrayDot"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6879dfe8-0276-0c7b-1806-d6b2b7035741"],
 " re-expresses a pairwise step in operand-local axes; ",
 Cell[BoxData["b"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7cc522fa-6a93-e579-24fa-bba40f27cc43"],
 "'s axis ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"b", "i"}], "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5b82e386-6ff5-c0ee-09b1-fae009819234"],
 " is the global slot ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["rank",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "+", 
   StyleBox["b", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "34a39a2f-b372-ffce-5c50-1388c604c514"],
 "."
}], "Item",
 CellID->2143439988,ExpressionUUID->"66ca9132-7812-8248-0ec9-097c79a4d092"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A repeated index that survives to the output is a broadcast (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["IndexedMultiply"]], 
    "paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/IndexedMultiply", 
    "Wolfram/TensorNetworks Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "023b1c4a-5b09-a8c9-33d8-96145ebdfa13"],
 "), not a contraction; a contracted index on three or more tensors is an ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "29a4f364-fd74-7ca4-5f5b-eb41f401468e"],
 "-element group or, in a contraction path, a batch index each step keeps \
while another tensor still carries it (",
